{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"docker.io/grafana/k6","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:08:34.559Z","source":{"name":"Docker Hub","api":"https://hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/grafana/k6/","page":"https://hub.docker.com/r/grafana/k6"},"readme":"**k6** is a modern load-testing tool, built on [our years of experience](https://k6.io/about) in the performance and testing industries.\nIt provides a clean, approachable scripting API, [local](https://docs.k6.io/docs/running-k6) and [cloud execution](https://docs.k6.io/docs/cloud-execution), flexible configuration, with command & control through CLI or a [REST API](https://docs.k6.io/docs/rest-api).\n\nThis is how load testing should look in the 21st century.\n\n---\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <img width=\"600\" src=\"https://github.com/grafana/k6/raw/master/assets/k6-demo.gif\">\n</p>\n\nAvailable Tags\n--------------\n\n- `latest`: the latest [released](https://github.com/grafana/k6/releases/latest) version of k6.\n- `latest-with-browser`: the latest [released](https://github.com/grafana/k6/releases/latest) version of k6 with [Browser API](https://k6.io/docs/javascript-api/k6-experimental/browser/) enabled.\n- `master`: current build of [k6 `master` branch](https://github.com/grafana/k6/tree/master).\n- `master-with-browser`: current build of [k6 `master` branch](https://github.com/grafana/k6/tree/master) with [Browser API](https://k6.io/docs/javascript-api/k6-experimental/browser/) enabled.\n- `X.Y.Z`: every [released version](https://github.com/grafana/k6/releases) of k6 is is available via a `X.Y.Z` tag, e.g. to use `k6@0.46.0` use `grafana/k6:0.46.0`.\n- `X.Y.Z-with-browser`: starting from `0.46.0` every k6 image is accompanied by an image that includes [Chromium](https://www.chromium.org/Home/) browser and has [Browser API](https://k6.io/docs/javascript-api/k6-experimental/browser/) enabled. Due to their size and privileges requirement (see \"A note on running browser tests\" below), they are provided as separate tags with `-with-browser` suffix. That is, to run your browser-based test with `k6@0.46.0` use the `grafana/k6:0.46.0-with-browser` image.\n\nFeatures\n--------\n\n- **Scripting in ES6 JS**: support for [modules](https://docs.k6.io/docs/modules) to aid code reusability across an organization\n- **Everything as code**: test logic and [configuration options](https://docs.k6.io/docs/options) are both in JS for version control friendliness\n- **Automation-friendly**: [checks](https://docs.k6.io/docs/checks) (like asserts) and [thresholds](https://docs.k6.io/docs/thresholds) for easy and flexible CI configuration!\n- [**HTTP/1.1**](https://docs.k6.io/docs/http-requests), [**HTTP/2**](https://docs.k6.io/docs/http2) and [**WebSocket**](https://docs.k6.io/docs/websockets) protocol support\n- **TLS features**: [client certificates](https://docs.k6.io/docs/ssl-tls-client-certificates), [configurable SSL/TLS versions and ciphers](https://docs.k6.io/docs/ssl-tls-version-and-cipher-suites)\n- **Batteries included**: [Cookies](https://docs.k6.io/docs/cookies), [Crypto](https://docs.k6.io/docs/k6crypto), [Custom metrics](https://docs.k6.io/docs/result-metrics#section-custom-metrics), [Encodings](https://docs.k6.io/docs/k6encoding), [Environment variables](https://docs.k6.io/docs/environment-variables), JSON, [HTML forms](https://docs.k6.io/docs/working-with-html-forms), [files](https://docs.k6.io/docs/open-filepath-mode), [flexible execution control](https://docs.k6.io/docs/running-k6#section-stages-ramping-updown-vus), and more.\n- **Built-in HAR converter**: record browser sessions as [`.har` files](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/.har) and [directly convert them to k6 scripts](https://docs.k6.io/docs/session-recording-har-support)\n- **Flexible metrics storage and visualization**: [Grafana dashboards](https://k6.io/docs/results-output/grafana-dashboards/) (InfluxDB, TimescaleDB, Prometheus Remote Write or AWS Timestream), [JSON](https://docs.k6.io/docs/results-output#section-json-output) or [Grafana Cloud](https://k6.io/docs/results-output/real-time/cloud/)\n- [**Cloud execution**](https://docs.k6.io/docs/cloud-execution) and distributed tests _(currently only on infrastructure managed by [Grafana Cloud](https://grafana.com/products/cloud/), with native distributed execution in k6 [planned]((https://github.com/orgs/grafana/projects/443/views/1)) for the near future!)_\n\nThere's even more! [See all features available in k6 docs](https://k6.io/docs/)\n\nUsage\n-----\n\nSee the Docker examples in the [Running k6 guide](https://k6.io/docs/get-started/running-k6/) to learn how to run tests using the `grafana/k6` images.\n\n### A note on running browser tests\n\nWhen running browser tests using the `*-with-browser` images, you'd need to provide additional capabilities to the container due to `k6` running Chrome in a sandbox mode:\n- Via Jessie Frazelle's [seccomp profile](https://github.com/jfrazelle/dotfiles/tree/master/etc/docker/seccomp/chrome.json) for Chrome:\n  Download:\n  ```\n  curl -o chrome.json https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jfrazelle/dotfiles/master/etc/docker/seccomp/chrome.json\n  ```\n  Launch the container using:\n  ```\n  docker run --rm -i --security-opt seccomp=$(pwd)/chrome.json grafana/k6:latest-with-browser - <script.js\n  ```\n- Provice `SYS_ADMIN` capability when running a container:\n  ```\n  docker run --rm -i --cap-add=SYS_ADMIN grafana/k6:latest-with-browser - <script.js\n  ```","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"vkarhaltsev","url":"https://hub.docker.com/u/grafana","official":false,"verified":false},"registered":"2022-02-04T14:25:55.715253Z","updated":"2026-09-25T09:04:20.205151Z","categories":["Developer tools"],"keywords":[],"license":null,"links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":31272096,"stars":43},"mediaTypes":["application/vnd.docker.container.image.v1+json","application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json"],"contentTypes":["image"],"storage":855626931337,"tags":[{"name":"master-with-browser","digest":"sha